# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the deployed directory
# (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml's "Stage deployable files" step, which
# copies it into dist/) and applies these headers at the edge.
#
# Raised 2026-08-29: rpg.burghertime.com kept showing a stale layout after a
# deploy that worked fine locally - confirmed via curl that the origin was
# serving the current, correct files the whole time, so the staleness was a
# browser holding onto its own locally-cached copy of css/js past a deploy.
# This project has no bundler - js/main.js transitively imports dozens of
# other files under js/, each cached at its own URL - so per-entry-point
# cache-busting (a version query string on just index.html's own two direct
# references) wouldn't reach most of the actual game code. `no-cache` here
# doesn't mean "don't cache" - it means "always revalidate with the origin
# before reusing the cached copy," which is a cheap conditional GET (a 304 if
# nothing changed) but guarantees a real change is picked up on next load
# instead of silently serving a copy from hours earlier.
/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
